## P0 — Project won't build/run (critical missing files)

- [x] **Restore `package.json`** — Reconstructed from `.package-lock.json` metadata. Added `@types/node` (missing from original). Clean `npm install` needed (original node_modules had CRLF bin scripts + missing platform binaries).
- [x] **Restore `vite.config.ts`** — Uses `fileURLToPath` (no `@types/node` `__dirname` needed), PWA plugin, vitest config via `/// <reference types="vitest/config" />`.
- [x] **Restore `index.html`** — Full-bleed game canvas, PWA meta tags, viewport lock.
- [x] **Fix `.gitignore`** — Added `dist/`, cleaned up Ralph generic entries.
- [ ] **Initialize git repo** — Needs user approval for `git init`.

## P1 — Build verification

- [x] **`npm run build`** — TypeScript type-check + Vite build passes. 109 modules, 1.9MB bundle (Phaser is big). PWA service worker generated.
- [x] **`npm test`** — 68 test files, 467 tests, all passing in 2.59s.
- [ ] **`npm run dev`** — Not tested (headless environment).

## P2 — Issues from REVISION_NOTES.md (flagged for review)

- [x] Boss collision radii are generic — tour bus at 96×96 may need dedicated radius. Corrected per-boss radii to match sprite body geometry: gordon=30, the_laird=28, hunter_general=28, taxman=30. Tour_bus already had 42. Generic `boss*` fallback (32) kept for future bosses.
- [x] Haggis body tilt simulated, not true rotation — cosmetic issue at larger scales. **Won't fix**: reads well at 56×56 game scale. True rotation requires RenderTexture pipeline — disproportionate effort for cosmetic-only benefit. Revisit only if character select screen ships with large sprites.
- [x] `terrier` texture key still says "terrier" despite drawing a midge — confusing for contributors. Renamed `terrier` → `midge` across all source files (enemies.ts, BootScene.ts, Enemy.ts, biomes.ts, BalanceConfig.ts, MenuScene.ts, MainMenuScene.ts, SpriteExportScene.ts, test). Display name now "Highland Midge".
- [x] Generic `boss` fallback (72×72) never tested — add console warning when used. Added `console.warn` in `Enemy.spawn()` when `config.texture === 'boss'`.

## Learnings

- Project has no `@/` path alias usage in source despite tsconfig defining it.
- `virtual:pwa-register` import in `main.ts` requires `vite-plugin-pwa`.
- `src/tools/SpriteExportScene.ts` exists for dev sprite export tool.
- All sprites are procedurally generated in `BootScene` — no external image assets.
